# Pray for divine aid while carrying more favour than an int16 holds, and
# photograph what the god grants. (bd inc-pf0p)
#
# Character::Pray (src/Prayer.cpp:1037) read the favour total into an int16
# local with an explicit cast off calcFavour(), which returns int32:
#
#     int16 retry, i, j, k, cFavour;      /* was */
#     cFavour = (int16)calcFavour(e.eID); /* was */
#
# Every row of the god's AID_CHART is then gated on that value. Past 32767 the
# cast wrapped NEGATIVE -- 120000 becomes -11072 -- so every threshold
# comparison read `threshold > -11072`, took the `continue`, and the follower
# received nothing at all. The symptom is silent: the prayer still charges the
# timeout and the favour penalty, and the god's own MSG_PRAYER still prints.
#
# THE SAME CHARACTER AS tools/keys/favour-int32.keys, and for the same reason:
# the wizard menu's "Become Divine Champion" (src/Debug.cpp:1118) sets one
# sacrifice category to 30000, and Hesani's EV_CALC_FAVOUR handler
# (lib/religion.irh:2170) multiplies it to 120000 for a level-one
# non-barbarian. That is the cheapest route in the game to a favour total past
# the wrap. Hesani's AID_CHART (lib/religion.irh:1994) opens AID_REFRESH at
# threshold 100 and AID_MANA at 0, both P_LOW, so a fresh champion qualifies
# for both on his first prayer.
#
# NO INJURY IS NEEDED. Creature::getTroubles (src/Prayer.cpp:682) reports
# TROUBLE_LOWMANA from the mana RATIO rather than a deficit, so a character at
# full mana already carries a P_LOW trouble; fatigue arrives the same way. That
# is why this script can pray the moment the character exists.
#
# 'p' IS LOWERCASE. StandardKeySet stores { KY_CMD_PRAY, 'P', 0 }
# (src/Tables.cpp:4755), but flag 0 means the UNSHIFTED key. An uppercase P is
# swallowed on the map with no message at all, which is how the first draft of
# this script measured a prayer that never happened.
#
# Seed 5 and tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat are part of the
# measurement, because every choice below is a menu letter and menu letters
# move when a list changes. tools/check_pray_aid_int32.sh supplies both.

@include dequ-setup.keys

@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Become Divine Champion"
H e s a n i
ENTER

# Ten blessings arrive at once, each behind a "-- more --" prompt, and the last
# of them leaves a dialog that swallows the next keystroke. Opening the sheet
# and leaving it again is what reliably returns us to the map.
@while "more --" SPACE
d
DOWN*20
ESC

p
@expect "Request aid"
a
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:prayed
@quit
